From 2ce727f74ebc6bf95d76fb59209f698d4b7d1fe3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@local>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 04:17:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add SDIO/FatFs SD card logging + AppModule scalability
 refactor

- SDCard.c/.h: SDIO block driver (4-bit bus, PC8-11/PC12/PD2) wrapping HAL_SD
- diskio.c/.h + ffconf.h: FatFs glue layer (FatFs core ff.c/ff.h must be
  added separately as third-party middleware - see ffconf.h header comment)
- DataLogger.c/.h: non-blocking SD CSV logger with RAM queue decoupling
  the SD card's blocking I/O from the 100 Hz IMU loop and FL FSM
- AppModule.c/.h: fixed-size module table replacing the hand-sequenced
  main loop, so new subsystems register instead of editing the loop body
- main.c: wraps existing subsystems as AppModule_t entries, wires in
  DataLogger, adds 'l'/'f' UART commands for log stats/flush
- stm32f4xx_hal_conf.h: enables HAL_SD_MODULE_ENABLED (was off)
- Makefile/CMakeLists.txt: new sources + HAL_SD/LL_SDMMC, conditional
  FatFs core inclusion
- README.md/CubeMX_Config_Guide.txt: SDIO wiring, memory budget update
